// EXPECT: PASS
// Phase-7 fragment-gate soundness demo, the FAIL-CLOSED direction. This postcondition is TRUE — for a
// nonnegative i64, an arithmetic right shift stays nonnegative — so with z3 present the check PASSES.
// But the obligation lowers to `bvashr` (and a `bvurem` shift-amount wrap), whose bit-blasts are NOT in
// the machine-checked fragment. So under `ANUBIS_NATIVE_AUTHORITATIVE=1` with z3 REMOVED from PATH, the
// native lane DECLINES (fragment gate → defer) and, with no z3 to fall through to, the check FAILS
// CLOSED rather than certify a property on an unproven blast. That is the whole point of the gate: a
// z3-free native proof rests only on proven wiring. (Contrast int_contract_proves.anb, which proves
// z3-free because every op it touches — bvadd + comparators — is machine-checked.)
pub fn ashr_keeps_sign(x: i64) -> i64
    requires(x >= 0)
    ensures(result >= 0)
{
    return x >> 1;
}

fn main() {
    print(0);
}
